c19494858493ad4d79fdaf309b18afd52bf4bbe","commits":[],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","finding_commits":{},"parent":"ec19494858493ad4d79fdaf309b18afd52bf4bbe","patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","tree":"f65110c09a9193ed5e7008eb3d786eacf8bfd3b8"},"dispositions":{"comments":[{"body":"[P2] [General] Limit the address fallback to the authority\n\nThis passes the database path and query to `parseMariaAddress`, whose port matcher searches the entire argument when there is no second `,address=`. Consequently, the valid URL `jdbc:mysql://address=(host=db.example)/(port=1234)` now reports `server.port=1234`, although the connection uses the default port 3306. The same happens with an ordinary database name and `?connectionAttributes=tag:(port=1234)`, and the MariaDB branch is also affected. Restrict the fallback to the first address block within the authority so database names and query values cannot supply host/port fields, and cover an omitted address port with address-like text outside the authority.","line":90,"path":"instrumentation/jdbc/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/jdbc/internal/parser/MysqlUrlParser.java","side":"RIGHT"}],"input_identity":{"pr_diff_sha256":"fda96a56ec3c746c68c694d8344649efdd7138b2291bb5d7b80cf087cc114150"},"outcome":"comments","request_digest":"9989f139a33aaea6868b2090aa1c41f17337d1331bfdbe670e7b5a574d9c1fe5","schema":2},"download_sha256":"d925fd77cf9c3daf5e6ec2f72f7a2ef02f7fb12b4b1648758167daaf64645422","frozen_sha":"ec19494858493ad4d79fdaf309b18afd52bf4bbe","pr":20660,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"9989f139a33aaea6868b2090aa1c41f17337d1331bfdbe670e7b5a574d9c1fe5","request_id":"e6e0fbd9f79741f9b4bf472278902841","run_attempt":1,"run_id":39056192757,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server